  "texts": {
    "P-005": {
      "note": "User re-entered VRT with 3sh (~$964 notional) in the 22:10 run -- larger than the $500 proposal but directionally matches; funding came from wallet cash broadly (multiple buys this run), not a dedicated TSM trim (TSM qty unchanged at 6sh). | TICKER CORRECTED 2026-08-15 (G77): was TSM, is VRT. The 2026-07-29 backfill parsed the action 'Re-enter VRT (funded by TSM trim)' and took the LAST caps token, which is the funding leg inside the parenthetical, not the subject. price_at_proposal $305.87 was never corrupt -- it is VRT's price on 2026-07-14 (VRT traded $287.53-$317.18 that week); it only looked impossible when read against TSM, which traded $386-$448. direction_bucket corrected TRIM->BUY: the proposal's subject action is re-entering VRT. This proposal's own note already recorded that the TSM leg never happened ('TSM qty unchanged at 6sh')."
    },
    "P-018": {
      "rationale": "New Power/DC name, selected from a 10-name screen. Chosen over HUBB/ETN/NVT/PWR/VST because it is GENERATION, not equipment: GEV and VRT are both equipment vendors sharing one order-book cycle, so a third equipment name adds a ticker without adding diversification. CEG sells power to datacenters under long-dated nuclear PPAs -- contracted revenue that keeps paying if AI capex pauses, which is the live risk. ATR20 3.58% (2nd lowest of the screen), 27.1% upside (double HUBB's), -3.61% on 28 Jul vs SMH -3.58%. Repairs the Power/DC floor breach (8.52% vs 10% floor) and lifts the cluster's equity ceiling from $29,870 to $56,550, removing Power as the binding constraint on total deployment. RISK: reports ~10 Aug, ~2 weeks of clean runway."
    },
    "P-064": {
      "rationale": "2.80x ATR risk cap, the largest excess in the book (~$1,222 headroom deficit) -- this trigger is independent of the earnings framing below and holds regardless. CORRECTED 2026-08-10 (user-flagged): FQ4 FY2026 (reported 08-05) was a BEAT -- revenue/EPS both topped consensus, record 84.6% gross margin, Data Center revenue +437% YoY, $93.9B in new multi-year agreements covering ~50% of 2027 bit production. The stock fell because FQ1 FY2027 guide came in below the Street's own elevated estimate, not because of a demand miss -- the 2-day post-earnings reaction was -10.2%, the rest of the ~-29.8% 1-month decline (G57, resolved) is late-July CXMT-selloff carryover shared across the whole Memory cluster. This is a sizing trim on a volatile, oversized position with genuinely strong underlying fundamentals -- not a vote against the business."
    },
    "P-105": {
      "rationale": "New live trigger, engine addendum: BofA downgraded Broadcom's BOND rating (2026-08-11) over the XPV off-balance-sheet AI financing platform AVGO built with Blackstone/Apollo to fund Anthropic compute -- stress-test exposure up to $370bn at full 2028 buildout, ~$42bn extreme-loss case. AVGO is named directly in this downgrade, same as BX (already trimmed under P-101 on this same catalyst). Cap-independent -- AVGO carries $1,044 of ATR headroom and is not over cap. TENSION, surfaced not suppressed: AVGO also sits in rotation's accumulate bucket on a strengthening thesis (real Q2 beat, 48% revenue growth, AI +143%) -- the catalyst and the accumulate signal answer different questions (financing-structure tail risk vs. operating fundamentals). This does not cancel the trigger; sized at the standard 20% catalyst_threat fraction, lighter than a cap-breach trim would be, precisely because the fundamentals are not in question."
    },
